      "MELANIE: I'm sorry. I couldn't possibly...\nLYDIA: You did say birds?",
      "MELANIE: That's silly, isn't it? Teaching a bird to shock my aunt. That's just silly and childish. Maybe I ought to go join the other children.\nANNIE: All right then, here we go. Once! Twice! Three! Go get 'em, Cathy!",
      "MELANIE: Yes.\nANNIE: That's the darnest thing thing I've ever seen in my life.\nLYDIA: Are they gone?",
      "ANNIE: Children, they were only seagulls.\nCATHY: They must have been after the food, Mother.",
      "MELANIE: No, thank you.\nCATHY: Why didn't Annie stay for dinner?"
